  "item_results": [
    {
      "item_id": "36c50723-3b65-49f6-9d9b-70574cc9471c",
      "session_id": "AdditionalQuestions-36c50723-what-happened-to-salander-in-the-abandoned-fa",
      "trace_id": "7393accfca1806c7ece2a275bf432083",
      "output": {
        "question": "What happened to Salander in the abandoned factory?",
        "answer": "Salander was shot three times by Alexander Zalachenko in the abandoned brickworks. After she threw sand into Ronald Niedermann's eyes and hit his hand with a spade, she attempted to flee toward the woods. As she ran, Zalachenko fired at her: the first bullet struck her hip, the second hit her back and shoulder blade causing paralyzing pain, and the third bullet penetrated her skull near her left ear, causing massive trauma and immediate loss of consciousness [E1] [E2]. She survived these injuries and was later found by the police who had been alerted by her text message [E3] [E4].",
        "citations": [
          "[E1]",
          "[E2]",
          "[E3]",
          "[E4]"
        ],
        "reranked": [
          {
            "book": "The Girl Who Played with Fire",
            "book_file": "The Girl Who Played with Fire _ A Lisbeth Salander Novel -- Larsson, Stieg -- Millennium trilogy, bk_ 2, New York, 2009 -- Alfred A_ Knopf -- isbn13 9780307272300 -- 078fc916144df1e3707c069bbf984d06 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "The_Girl_who-ayed_with_Fire_split_072.html",
            "paragraph": 154,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": null,
            "page": "140",
            "text": "The fucking old man has a gun too .\nThe realization cracked like a whip through her mind.\nShe changed direction in the same instant the shot was fired. The bullet struck the outside of her hip and made her spin off balance.\nShe felt no pain.\nThe second bullet hit her in the back and stopped against her left shoulder blade. A paralyzing pain sliced through her body.\nShe went down on her knees. For a few seconds she could not move. She was conscious that Zalachenko was behind her, about twenty feet away. With one last surge of energy she stubbornly hurled herself to her feet and took a wobbly step towards the cover of the bushes.",
            "paragraph_end": 159,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "90974057c3ddd98b7e65fdd3202652eb230419df7586e9fd87a328d60847e011",
            "id": "90974057-c3dd-d98b-7e65-fdd3202652eb",
            "agent_label": "E1"
          },
          {
            "book": "The Girl Who Played with Fire",
            "book_file": "The Girl Who Played with Fire _ A Lisbeth Salander Novel -- Larsson, Stieg -- Millennium trilogy, bk_ 2, New York, 2009 -- Alfred A_ Knopf -- isbn13 9780307272300 -- 078fc916144df1e3707c069bbf984d06 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "The_Girl_who-ayed_with_Fire_split_072.html",
            "paragraph": 160,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": null,
            "page": "140",
            "text": "Zalachenko had time to aim.\nThe third bullet caught her about an inch below the top of her left ear. It penetrated her skull and caused a spiderweb of radial cracks in her cranium. The lead came to rest in the grey matter about two inches beneath the cerebral cortex, by the cerebrum.\nFor Salander the medical detail was academic. The bullet caused immediate massive trauma. Her last sensation was a glowing red shock that turned into a white light.",
            "paragraph_end": 162,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "95082038310d0f20d644b16ea7354b422afd424f6c1d5b8a56188d91805efb4d",
            "id": "95082038-310d-0f20-d644-b16ea7354b42",
            "agent_label": "E2"
          },
          {
            "book": "The Girl Who Kicked the Hornet's Nest",
            "book_file": "The Girl Who Kicked the Hornet's Nest -- Stieg Larsson -- Millennium Trilogy #3, 2010 -- Random House, Inc_ -- a9a1c0e6f4b8fd47fa0771ff9463bc34 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "OEBPS/Lars_9780307593672_epub_epl_r1.htm",
            "paragraph": 244,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "EPILOGUE: INVENTORY OF ESTATE Friday, December 2–Sunday, December 18",
            "page": null,
            "text": "When Nieminen and his pals had found the open door at the end of the building, she opened her mobile again. She composed a message and sent it to the police station in Norrtälje.\nCOP KILLER R. NIEDERMANN IN OLD BRICKWORKS BY THE GAS STATION OUTSIDE SKEDERID. ABOUT TO BE MURDERED BY S. NIEMINEN AND MEMBERS OF SVAVELSJÖ MC. WOMEN DEAD IN PIT ON GROUND FLOOR.\nShe could not see any movement from the factory.",
            "paragraph_end": 246,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "0b2e2b0631bc3153bc98aaf375c332696af69ddf5da6dadbf7eb278a09e58f22",
            "id": "0b2e2b06-31bc-3153-bc98-aaf375c33269",
            "agent_label": "E3"
          },
          {
            "book": "The Girl Who Kicked the Hornet's Nest",
            "book_file": "The Girl Who Kicked the Hornet's Nest -- Stieg Larsson -- Millennium Trilogy #3, 2010 -- Random House, Inc_ -- a9a1c0e6f4b8fd47fa0771ff9463bc34 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "OEBPS/Lars_9780307593672_epub_epl_r1.htm",
            "paragraph": 250,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "EPILOGUE: INVENTORY OF ESTATE Friday, December 2–Sunday, December 18",
            "page": null,
            "text": "Finally it was all over.\nThe story that had begun on the day she was born had ended at the brickworks.\nShe was free.\nWhen the officers took out assault rifles from their vehicles, put on Kevlar vests, and started to fan out around the factory site, Salander went inside the shop and bought a coffee and a sandwich wrapped in cellophane. She ate standing at a counter in the café.\nIt was dark by the time she got back to her car. Just as she opened the door, she heard two distant reports from what she assumed were handguns on the other side of the road. She saw several black figures, presumably policemen, pressed against the wall near the entrance at one end of the building. She heard sirens as another squad car approached from the direction of Uppsala. A few cars had stopped at the side of the road below her to watch the drama.",
            "paragraph_end": 254,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "72c4aa39d468e3b21bb5adf6ccb102597d92026af8eebd418a64ab046e434223",
            "id": "72c4aa39-d468-e3b2-1bb5-adf6ccb10259",
            "agent_label": "E4"
          }
        ],
